  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">223380_FY24_WFP_DRC - Kasai Emergency School Feeding</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Goal: Improved enrolment and attendance of boys and girls in targeted Miabi and Lupatapata territory in Kasai Oriental schools
 
 Outcome 1: Reduce immediate child hunger in targeted schools by providing daily food support
 
 Output 1.1 Increased access to daily school meal for 52,912 school going children in 76 schools (Kasai central, Kasai and Lomami.
 
 Output 1.2: Adequate storage and food preparation facilities maintained in the targeted schools
 
 Outcome 2: Increased knowledge, skills and general capacity on good nutrition practices and food production for targeted schools and students
 
 Output 2.1: Students in targeted schools are sensitized on good nutrition practices
 
 Output 2.2: Students in targeted schools are reached with deworming services
 
 Output 2.3. Target schools develop school gardens for diversification of meals
 
 Outcome 3: Increased accountability to communities.
 
 Output 3.1: Accountability mechanisms established/strengthened.
 
 Output 3.2: Protection mainstreamed in all aspects of programming</narrative>
  </description>
